      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "Model dissic and talk are stored per unit volume (mol m-3) while GLODAP is per unit mass, so converting to micromoles per kilogram for the requested means, biases and RMSE requires the density/scale-factor handling this fragment describes.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Convert per-volume to per-mass with µmol kg-1 = mmol m-3 × 1000 / ρ using the **in-situ** density (`compute_potential_density_anomaly` with `ref_pressure=None`) passed to `transform_unit`; its constant-density default errs ~1 % in the deep ocean and fresh polar water.",
        "State which density was used (result `attrs['density_assumption']`); never relabel mol m-3 × 1e3 as µmol kg-1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/common-comparison-mask.md",
      "sha256": "bbb98200f52b4a692ce097704b8c438179a795a44bec6b856c03cf31931af4ea",
      "reason": "The bias, RMSE and spatial correlation on the GLODAP 1-degree grid exist only where both model and GLODAP have data, and the depth-level biases must be averaged over cells where both are defined, exactly the mask rule this fragment states.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Put all fields on the GLODAP 1° grid, build one mask with `build_comparison_mask` and apply `.where(mask)` before any bias/RMSE/correlation; pass `ocean_only=False` because the reference is GLODAP, not WOA23 (WOA23's coastline would drop GLODAP ocean cells and flatter every model).",
        "Report the mask's cell counts; take means from `compute_difference_metrics` (`mean_data`, `mean_reference`) over the shared sample, not from separate means; for the depth profile use the cells shared at each depth, since a surface mask does not carry to another level."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices.md",
      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The 2002-minus-1971–2000 DIC change is an anomaly relative to a stated baseline period, so the fragment's rule that an anomaly is defined only relative to its baseline applies to computing and stating that change.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The 2002-minus-1971–2000 DIC change is internal to each model: against a field's own climatology its bias cancels, so the change is small relative to the GLODAP bias and the ratio does not make the bias a model error — state this when interpreting the ratio."
      ]
    },
    {
